{"id":"24aa74ef95a06c55","group":"68","path":"68/68-df-hypersimple-set.md","title":"Hypersimple Set","display":"df-hypersimple-set — Hypersimple Set","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)","book_abbrev":"68","label":"68-df-hypersimple-set","aliases":["68-df-hypersimple-set"],"display":"df-hypersimple-set — Hypersimple Set","depends_on":["[[68-df-recursive-function]]","[[68-df-recursively-enumerable-set]]"],"source_edition":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF","source_location":"§17 definition p.64 / PDF 73","verification_status":"source-statement-checked","source_proof_status":"not-checked"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"68"},{"key":"label","html":"68-df-hypersimple-set"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>68-df-hypersimple-set</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-hypersimple-set — Hypersimple Set"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a82d826d433dcff3\" href=\"?note=a82d826d433dcff3\" title=\"68-df-recursive-function\">68-df-recursive-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"913d52943499d039\" href=\"?note=913d52943499d039\" title=\"68-df-recursively-enumerable-set\">68-df-recursively-enumerable-set</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF"},{"key":"source_location","html":"§17 definition p.64 / PDF 73"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"not-checked"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\subseteq\\mathbb N\">\\(A\\subseteq\\mathbb N\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\overline A=\\mathbb N\\setminus A\">\\(\\overline A=\\mathbb N\\setminus A\\)</span>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RE}\">\\(\\mathrm{RE}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"913d52943499d039\" href=\"?note=913d52943499d039\" title=\"68-df-recursively-enumerable-set\">68-df-recursively-enumerable-set</a>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TotalRec}\">\\(\\mathrm{TotalRec}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"a82d826d433dcff3\" href=\"?note=a82d826d433dcff3\" title=\"68-df-recursive-function\">68-df-recursive-function</a>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb N^{\\mathbb N}\">\\(\\mathbb N^{\\mathbb N}\\)</span> 指全的一元数值函数空间。</p>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HyperSimple}\">\\(\\mathrm{HyperSimple}\\)</span> 为以下引入的集合性质谓词。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HyperSimple}(A)\\;\\Longleftrightarrow\\;A\\in\\mathrm{RE}\\land|\\overline A|=\\aleph_0\\land\\neg\\exists F\\in\\mathrm{TotalRec}\\cap\\mathbb N^{\\mathbb N}\\;\\forall x\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\exists y\\in\\mathbb N\\;(y\\notin A\\land x&lt;y&lt;F(x)).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{HyperSimple}(A)\\;\\Longleftrightarrow\\;A\\in\\mathrm{RE}\\land|\\overline A|=\\aleph_0\\land\\neg\\exists F\\in\\mathrm{TotalRec}\\cap\\mathbb N^{\\mathbb N}\\;\\forall x\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\exists y\\in\\mathbb N\\;(y\\notin A\\land x&lt;y&lt;F(x)).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>对应 §17，印刷 p.64 / PDF p.73。直接采用原书的递归区间界定义，避免旧稿在 Hypothesis 预先假设补集具有无限递增枚举，也不再把未经说明的枚举函数 a_n 当作原语。等价的“补集主函数不被递归函数最终支配”可另证，当前定义不依赖该等价。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"68-df-recursive-function","status":"resolved","id":"a82d826d433dcff3"